---
/**
 * Homepage — Approved Contractor, Inc. (concept build 005, "The Stamp").
 *
 * SUPERSEDES build 003, "The Elevation", 2026-08-09. That page answered an
 * empty intake by drawing a picture; this one was gathered first-hand and has
 * real material to work with. See engine/docs/differentiation-log.md.
 *
 * THE ONE-SENTENCE IDEA
 * ---------------------
 * Every contractor in California says they are approved. This is the one where
 * you can actually go and check — so the page is built as the record you check
 * it against, and their own stamp is what lands on it.
 *
 * The idea is structural, not decorative. It decides:
 *
 *   COLOUR    their own sampled stamp ink #ae0f15 as a FIELD, not an accent.
 *             The page alternates red → paper → red → paper, so the thing you
 *             remember about it is the colour of their logo.
 *   HERO      "Don't take our word for it. Take the state's." — the record
 *             line above it, one of their own job photographs mounted beside
 *             it as evidence.
 *   RECORD    the signature moment. Their actual CSLB licence record on a
 *             true-white card, and the stamp landing on it once.
 *   LEDGER    every other approval, grouped by who granted it and glossed with
 *             what it means, with a public lookup link wherever one exists.
 *             Not a badge wall.
 *   TYPE      a heavy roman against a light geometric sans, because that is
 *             exactly the contrast their own wordmark is built on.
 *
 * SECTION RHYTHM. Red hero → paper credentials → paper scope → RED RECORD →
 * paper work → paper process → paper reviews → paper questions → paper contact
 * → red close. The two red fields bracket the page and the record sits in the
 * middle of it. Build 003 alternated paper bands around a single dark title
 * block; nothing about this rhythm is shared with it.
 *
 * WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE (CLAUDE.md §11)
 * ----------------------------------------------
 *   NO AGGREGATE RATING, NO STAR COUNT, NO REVIEW TOTAL, anywhere on the page
 *   or in the JSON-LD. Five sources gave five irreconcilable numbers — their
 *   own site says "800+", GuildQuality 4.6 from 85, Houzz 4.7 from 77, Yelp
 *   125, and one aggregator claims 5.0 from 258 while attributing a review of
 *   a different company (input/facts.txt CONFLICT #4 and #5).
 *
 *   This is the single largest omission in the build and it is the point: on a
 *   page whose whole argument is "go and check us", an uncheckable "800+
 *   5-star reviews" is the one claim on it that would fail its own test.
 *
 *   NO HOURS. Not published by them anywhere; third-party listings disagree.
 *   showHours={false} and site.ts emits no openingHoursSpecification.
 *
 *   NO BORROWED MANUFACTURER LOGOS. Licensed to them, not to us.
 *
 *   NO PORTRAIT of Jared Green — none is published. He is named, not shown.
 */
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import HeroStamp from "../components/sections/HeroStamp.astro";
import CredentialLedger from "../components/sections/CredentialLedger.astro";
import ServicesGrid from "../components/sections/ServicesGrid.astro";
import TheRecord from "../components/sections/TheRecord.astro";
import BeforeAfter from "../components/sections/BeforeAfter.astro";
import Gallery from "../components/sections/Gallery.astro";
import ProcessSteps from "../components/sections/ProcessSteps.astro";
import TestimonialPullQuote from "../components/sections/TestimonialPullQuote.astro";
import TestimonialGrid from "../components/sections/TestimonialGrid.astro";
import ProviderBios from "../components/sections/ProviderBios.astro";
import FAQ from "../components/sections/FAQ.astro";
import LocationContact from "../components/sections/LocationContact.astro";
import CTABand from "../components/sections/CTABand.astro";

import heroPhoto from "../assets/photos/la-stucco-to-hardie-after.jpg";

import { SITE, LICENCE } from "../config/site";
import { localized } from "../lib/content";
import { useTranslations, localeFromUrl } from "../i18n/ui";

const locale = localeFromUrl(Astro.url);
const t = useTranslations(locale);

const services = await localized("services", locale);
const credentials = await localized("credentials", locale);
const process = await localized("process", locale);
const faqs = await localized("faq", locale);
const projects = await localized("projects", locale);
const reviews = await localized("testimonials", locale);
const people = await localized("people", locale);

/**
 * The record card.
 *
 * Every value read off the CSLB register on 2026-08-12 and held in site.ts's
 * LICENCE block, so the card, the FAQ answer and the footer cannot drift apart.
 * The status row is the only emphasised field — it is the one the whole page
 * exists to show.
 */
const recordFields = [
  { label: "Status", value: LICENCE.status, emphasis: true },
  { label: "Licence number", value: "952272" },
  { label: "Business name on record", value: LICENCE.businessName },
  { label: "Classification", value: LICENCE.classification },
  { label: "Entity", value: LICENCE.entity },
  { label: "Issued", value: LICENCE.issued },
  { label: "Expires", value: LICENCE.expires },
  { label: "Address on record", value: LICENCE.address },
  {
    label: "Contractor's bond",
    value: `${LICENCE.bondAmount} · ${LICENCE.bondCompany}`,
  },
  { label: "Workers' compensation", value: LICENCE.workersComp },
  { label: "Qualifying individual", value: LICENCE.qualifier },
];

/** The featured pair, and everything else. BeforeAfter filters to pairs itself. */
const pairs = projects.filter((p) => p.data.beforePhoto);
const singles = projects.filter((p) => !p.data.beforePhoto);

const galleryItems = singles.map((p) => ({
  image: p.data.photo!,
  alt: p.data.alt!,
  caption: p.data.location
    ? `${p.data.title} · ${p.data.location}`
    : p.data.title,
}));

const featuredReview = reviews.find((r) => r.data.featured);
const otherReviews = reviews.filter((r) => !r.data.featured);

const callLabel = `${t("cta.call")} ${SITE.phone}`;
const callHref = `tel:${SITE.phoneHref}`;

const navLinks = [
  { label: "The record", href: "#record" },
  { label: "What they do", href: "#services" },
  { label: "The work", href: "#work" },
  { label: "Questions", href: "#faq" },
  { label: "Contact", href: "#contact" },
];

/** FAQPage JSON-LD — only ever emitted for Q&As the page visibly renders. */
const faqSchema = faqs.map((f) => ({
  question: f.data.question,
  answer: f.data.answer,
}));
---

{/* SEOHead prefixes SITE.name on the homepage, so `title` must not repeat it. */}
<BaseLayout
  title="Siding, windows, stucco & roofing — licensed in California since 2010"
  description="Exterior only: James Hardie siding, Andersen and Pella windows, stucco, texture coating, roofing and shutters. Canoga Park, CA. CSLB licence #952272, current and active. Free consultation — (877) 792-9082."
  path="/"
  navLinks={navLinks}
  faq={faqSchema}
  announcement={{
    /* Short enough to hold ONE line at 390px. The two-line version cost 25px
       of a phone viewport that the hero needed to keep its primary CTA clear
       of the concept badge. Their own bar reads "UPGRADE NOW, PAY LATER -
       Call Us for Details", so this is also closer to their wording. */
    message: "Upgrade now, pay later — 12 months no interest.",
    href: "#contact",
    linkLabel: "Ask about financing",
    id: "finance-2026",
  }}
>
  <HeroStamp
    record="CSLB #952272 · Current and active · Class B · Issued 2010"
    headingLead="Don't take our word for it."
    headingTurn="Take the state's."
    body="Siding, windows, stucco, texture coating, roofing and shutters — the outside of the house, and nothing else. Licence, bond and workers' compensation are all public record. The lookup takes about thirty seconds."
    photo={heroPhoto}
    photoAlt="The rear elevation of a two-storey Los Angeles house finished in pale James Hardie lap siding, with white trim, dark shutters and a screened porch."
    captionPlace="Los Angeles, CA"
    captionWork="Stucco removed, James Hardie lap siding installed"
    ctaHref="#contact"
    ctaLabel="Book a free consultation"
    telHref={callHref}
    telLabel={callLabel}
  />

  {/*
    THE SIGNATURE MOMENT, placed high on purpose.
    Conventionally the proof section sits late, after the sell. Here the proof
    IS the sell, so it runs second — before the services, before the work,
    before anything asks for a call. Everything after it is detail.
  */}
  <TheRecord
    id="record"
    eyebrow="The public record"
    heading="The company is called Approved Contractor. Here is the approval."
    body="This is their licence as the State of California holds it, not as they describe it. We looked it up rather than take their word for it, and so can you."
    authority={LICENCE.authority}
    documentTitle={LICENCE.documentTitle}
    fields={recordFields}
    retrieval={`Retrieved from cslb.ca.gov on ${LICENCE.retrieved}. Bond and policy dates move — check the live record.`}
    verifyHref={LICENCE.lookupUrl}
    verifyLabel="Look up licence 952272 yourself →"
  />

  <CredentialLedger
    id="credentials"
    eyebrow="Everyone else who has checked"
    heading="Nine more approvals, and who granted each one."
    body="A row of logos proves nothing — anyone can paste a logo. These are the actual designations, the bodies that issue them, and where you can look them up."
    items={credentials}
    featureLabel="James Hardie Elite Contractor"
    footnote="Manufacturer and award marks are the property of the organisations that issue them and are named here in text rather than reproduced. Where a designation could not be confirmed from a public source, the entry says so."
    tone="sunken"
  />

  <ServicesGrid
    id="services"
    eyebrow="The whole scope"
    heading="Six trades, all of them outdoors."
    body="Approved Contractor is not a general remodeler. There is no kitchen, no bathroom and no addition on this list, and that is the point — everything here is the building envelope."
    items={services}
    columns={3}
    media="none"
  />

  {
    pairs.length > 0 && (
      <BeforeAfter
        id="work"
        eyebrow="The same house, twice"
        heading="Stucco off, James Hardie on."
        body="One project in Los Angeles, photographed before the work started and after it finished."
        items={pairs}
        tone="sunken"
      />
    )
  }

  {
    galleryItems.length > 0 && (
      <Gallery
        locale={locale}
        eyebrow="Recent work"
        heading="Five more, across six counties."
        items={galleryItems}
        layout="uniform"
        tone="sunken"
        spacing="tight"
      />
    )
  }

  <ProcessSteps
    id="process"
    eyebrow="What happens when you call"
    heading="Four steps, in their own words."
    body="Quoted from Approved Contractor's own description of how a job runs, rather than rewritten into ours."
    steps={process}
    layout="row"
    ctaLabel={callLabel}
    ctaHref={callHref}
  />

  {/* Explicit id below: TestimonialPullQuote and TestimonialGrid BOTH default
      to id="reviews", so leaving it off shipped two elements sharing an id —
      invalid HTML, and it breaks any in-page anchor to either of them. */}
  {
    featuredReview && (
      <TestimonialPullQuote
        id="review-featured"
        locale={locale}
        eyebrow="A customer, at length"
        testimonial={featuredReview}
        tone="sunken"
      />
    )
  }

  {
    otherReviews.length > 0 && (
      <TestimonialGrid
        locale={locale}
        eyebrow="Verified surveys"
        heading="What people said afterwards."
        body="Collected by GuildQuality, which surveys a contractor's customers directly and publishes the unhappy ones too. No star average is shown here because no two sources agree on one."
        items={otherReviews}
        columns={3}
      />
    )
  }

  {
    people.length > 0 && (
      <ProviderBios
        id="owner"
        eyebrow="Who is responsible"
        heading="There is a name on the licence."
        body="In a trade where the fear is that whoever took the deposit will not answer the phone, the state requires a specific person to stand behind the work. On licence 952272 that person is named."
        people={people}
        layout="feature"
        tone="sunken"
      />
    )
  }

  <FAQ
    id="faq"
    locale={locale}
    eyebrow="Before you call"
    heading="The questions people actually ask."
    items={faqs}
  />

  <LocationContact
    id="contact"
    locale={locale}
    eyebrow="Canoga Park"
    heading="Where the trucks go out from."
    body="9015 Eton Avenue — the address on the licence, not a mailbox. Serving Los Angeles, San Diego, Orange, Ventura, San Bernardino and Riverside counties."
    showHours={false}
    tone="sunken"
    formSubject="Exterior consultation request"
  />

  <CTABand
    heading="Have someone look at the outside of your house."
    body="Free consultation, and no obligation after it. Tell them what is bothering you about the exterior and they will tell you what is actually failing."
    ctaLabel={callLabel}
    ctaHref={callHref}
    secondaryLabel="Check the licence first"
    secondaryHref={LICENCE.lookupUrl}
    note="CA Lic. #952272 · Class B · Current and active · Financing available"
    align="split"
    tone="brand"
  />
</BaseLayout>

{
  /*
  ============================================================================
  OPEN ITEMS — CLOSE THESE BEFORE SENDING
  ============================================================================
  Full detail, with sources and conflicts, is in input/facts.txt §15.

  ONLY THE BUSINESS CAN CLOSE THESE:

  1. A PORTRAIT OF JARED GREEN. He is named on the page and on the state
     licence record, but no photograph of him is published anywhere. In this
     trade a face is the single highest-trust element available, and it is now
     the biggest remaining gap — the photography gap that dogged builds 002,
     003 and 004 is otherwise closed.

  2. HOURS. Not published by them. Third-party listings disagree on Saturday.
     site.ts HOURS is empty, showHours={false}, no openingHoursSpecification.

  3. AN EMAIL ADDRESS. Not published; SITE.email empty, so the block is omitted.

  4. THE PHONE CONFLICT. Their homepage header shows (866) 215-2968 while their
     contact page, about page AND the CSLB register all show (877) 792-9082.
     This page uses the register's number. Worth raising with them either way:
     a header number that disagrees with the licence record is a trust leak on
     a page whose whole subject is trust.

  5. THE REVIEW COUNT. If they can point at ~800 verified reviews on ONE
     platform, the number goes straight back on the page — it is a good number.
     Right now five sources give five answers.

  6. YELP AND GOOGLE REVIEWS. Yelp shows 125 reviews and Google shows more;
     both were unreadable to us. Ten minutes of copy-and-paste would materially
     strengthen the testimonial section. One Google review in particular —
     a customer saying they chose Approved Contractor because the rep
     "provided full license and insurance info" — is the thesis of this entire
     redesign in a customer's own words, and it is left off only because the
     aggregator carrying it is provably contaminated. See input/reviews.txt §3.

  7. AWARD CURRENCY. The Qualified Remodeler Top 500 and HIP 200 badges say
     2025. Confirm they are current for 2026 or the year stays on them.

  8. FINANCING TERMS. Read 2026-08-12. Promotional finance offers move
     constantly; re-check before this is sent.

  ENGINEERING, BEFORE ANY CLIENT TEST:

  9. FORM_ENDPOINT is empty, so ContactForm renders its disabled state.

 10. GEO COORDINATES. site.ts `geo` is null, so LocalBusiness omits it rather
     than pin the wrong unit on Eton Avenue.

  CONSIDERED AND DECLINED:

 11. SPANISH. The Valley has a large Spanish-speaking homeowner base and
     bilingual would be a genuine differentiator here. Declined for this pass:
     every word of a licensed trade's advertising has to be the operator's own,
     not a machine translation. One content pass if wanted.

 12. AN AGGREGATE RATING. Declined permanently unless a single source can be
     established. See the header note.
  ============================================================================
  */
}
